WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:05.040
The Stargate franchise spans three&nbsp;
decades, three TV shows, and three movies,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.040 --> 00:00:09.280
plus other non-canon material. Want&nbsp;
to know where to start? We've got you&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:09.280 --> 00:00:13.280
covered. This is the correct order in&nbsp;
which to watch the Stargate franchise.

00:00:14.400 --> 00:00:18.800
Any Stargate watch-through should&nbsp;
logically begin with the 1994 movie.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:18.800 --> 00:00:23.760
It's the film that launched the entire franchise,&nbsp;
and it's the first time audiences were introduced&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:23.760 --> 00:00:28.880
to the Stargate universe. The plot builds on&nbsp;
the popular conspiracy that aliens built the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:28.880 --> 00:00:34.240
pyramids in Giza, Egypt and proceeds to create&nbsp;
a mythology around the wide-ranging implications&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:34.240 --> 00:00:37.520
of that central concept.
Played by James Spader,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:37.520 --> 00:00:42.240
the main protagonist of the original movie&nbsp;
is an archaeologist named Daniel Jackson.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:42.240 --> 00:00:46.720
He is a confirmed believer in the theory that&nbsp;
aliens built the massive ancient structures.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:46.720 --> 00:00:52.960
Not surprisingly, academia at large rejects and&nbsp;
ostracizes Daniel. But as it always tends to be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:52.960 --> 00:00:58.240
with crackpot academics in movies: Jackson&nbsp;
is more correct than he could possibly know.&nbsp;

00:00:58.240 --> 00:01:03.360
The U.S. military has managed to get their hands&nbsp;
on an alien device buried in the sands of Egypt,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:03.360 --> 00:01:09.040
which is dubbed the Stargate. Eventually, Jackson&nbsp;
teams up with Colonel Jack O'Neill, played&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:09.040 --> 00:01:14.720
perfectly stoically by Kurt Russell. Together&nbsp;
they work to uncover the secrets of the Stargate.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:14.720 --> 00:01:19.520
As it turns out, this large ring-like&nbsp;
device is basically a universal phone.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:19.520 --> 00:01:23.040
You “dial” a set of coordinates in 3D&nbsp;
space, and if there's a connection,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:23.040 --> 00:01:28.000
you can transport yourself to another planet.
Unfortunately for Jackson, O'Neill, and their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:28.000 --> 00:01:34.000
team, this is no vacation. On this new world, they&nbsp;
quickly become embroiled in an age-old conflict.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:34.000 --> 00:01:39.840
They must defeat an evil alien dictator that calls&nbsp;
himself Ra before they can return home to Earth.

00:01:41.200 --> 00:01:45.840
After finishing the movie, you get to enjoy&nbsp;
a long uninterrupted stretch of television&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:45.840 --> 00:01:50.720
in the form of Stargate SG-1. The series&nbsp;
spans ten seasons overall, but for now,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:50.720 --> 00:01:55.760
we're just going to focus on the first seven. SG-1&nbsp;
is a spin-off from the original film, and picks up&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:55.760 --> 00:02:00.400
roughly one year after the events of the movie.&nbsp;
In the pilot, the Stargate device activates on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:00.400 --> 00:02:05.440
its own, and aliens walk through, killing and&nbsp;
kidnapping several U.S. military personnel.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:05.440 --> 00:02:09.120
Naturally the government reacts by setting&nbsp;
up a secret base called Stargate Command&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:09.120 --> 00:02:15.680
to monitor the device and mount a rescue mission.
The base is led by General Hammond, played by the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:15.680 --> 00:02:20.960
always authoritative Don Davis, who pulls Jack&nbsp;
O'Neill, now played by Richard Dean Anderson,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:20.960 --> 00:02:25.760
out of retirement. From there, O'Neill makes&nbsp;
contact with and once again recruits Daniel&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:25.760 --> 00:02:30.880
Jackson, played by Michael Shanks. He completes&nbsp;
his team with the very capable Samantha Carter,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:30.880 --> 00:02:34.720
as played by Amanda Tapping, and&nbsp;
ultimately the renegade Goa'uld&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:34.720 --> 00:02:40.320
warrior Teal'c, as depicted by Christopher Judge.
The show quickly establishes that the Goa'uld are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:40.320 --> 00:02:46.720
an aggressive, highly advanced alien civilization&nbsp;
who are bent on destroying and enslaving humanity.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:46.720 --> 00:02:52.160
To protect Earth, Stargate Command assembles a&nbsp;
group of teams, led by SG-1, to travel through&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:52.160 --> 00:02:56.800
the Stargate, exploring the universe and searching&nbsp;
for allies in the battle against their new foe.&nbsp;

00:02:57.360 --> 00:03:02.320
Each episode has SG-1 visiting new locations&nbsp;
looking for partners and technology that will give&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:02.320 --> 00:03:07.040
them the edge over the Goa'uld, but interesting&nbsp;
storylines develop as the show progresses.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:08.000 --> 00:03:13.200
In the first seven seasons, the four-person team&nbsp;
of SG-1 operates out of a secret base in Colorado,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:13.200 --> 00:03:18.000
traveling to other planets and facing&nbsp;
down all manner of alien threats.

00:03:18.000 --> 00:03:22.800
After wrapping up season 7, things start to get&nbsp;
a little more complicated. While Stargate SG-1&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:22.800 --> 00:03:28.000
was still in production, MGM took advantage of&nbsp;
its popularity and launched a spinoff TV series&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:28.000 --> 00:03:32.640
called Stargate Atlantis. Both of the shows&nbsp;
took place in the same fictional universe,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:32.640 --> 00:03:38.160
and their stories run in parallel to each other.
The good news is that SG-1 and Atlantis are mostly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:38.160 --> 00:03:42.560
independent from each other. They take place in&nbsp;
different galaxies and have entirely different&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:42.560 --> 00:03:48.080
storylines and casts. But there are a few episodes&nbsp;
where the shows reference each other in some way.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:48.080 --> 00:03:51.520
You won't have to weave the episodes&nbsp;
together, but it's probably best to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:51.520 --> 00:03:56.640
start watching Stargate SG-1 season 8 and&nbsp;
Stargate Atlantis season 1 at the same time.&nbsp;

00:03:57.520 --> 00:04:01.920
The climax of Stargate SG-1 season 7&nbsp;
introduces the lost city of Atlantis.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:02.480 --> 00:04:06.240
The SG-1 team discovers its&nbsp;
location, lost in deep space.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:07.120 --> 00:04:11.840
Stargate Command sends a permanent team there,&nbsp;
which sets up a base and lives as a colony in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:11.840 --> 00:04:17.520
the lost city. Stargate SG-1 season 8 continues&nbsp;
the storyline, and by the season finale, the team&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:17.520 --> 00:04:23.120
finally defeats its two biggest opponents: The&nbsp;
Goa'uld and the Replicators. Meanwhile, Stargate&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:23.120 --> 00:04:28.080
Atlantis introduces several new characters as&nbsp;
well as the team's own powerful enemy, the Wraith.

00:04:29.760 --> 00:04:34.480
Continuing on with the trend, your next step&nbsp;
should be to watch Stargate SG-1 season 9 along&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:34.480 --> 00:04:39.120
with Stargate Atlantis season 2. Once again,&nbsp;
you don't need to go back and forth between&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:39.120 --> 00:04:43.680
the two shows, but it will help to watch them&nbsp;
back-to-back since the events that occur in them&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:43.680 --> 00:04:47.040
take place at the same time.
With many long-running series,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:47.040 --> 00:04:52.560
established characters enter and leave depending&nbsp;
on off-screen events, and season 9 was a massive&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:52.560 --> 00:04:58.320
change for SG-1. Both Jack O'Neill and General&nbsp;
Hammond transition into supporting characters who&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:58.320 --> 00:05:03.680
play minor roles in the series. They are replaced&nbsp;
by Beau Bridges' Hank Landry, new commander&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:03.680 --> 00:05:10.160
of Stargate Command, and Ben Browder as Cameron&nbsp;
Mitchell, the new leader of a fractured SG-1 team.&nbsp;

00:05:10.160 --> 00:05:14.000
Additionally, Vala Mal Doran, a recurring&nbsp;
character played by Claudia Black,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:14.000 --> 00:05:19.200
becomes a primary member of the SG-1&nbsp;
team. Mal Doran is an extremely clever,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:19.200 --> 00:05:24.080
though morally dubious human alien with&nbsp;
a deep infatuation with Daniel Jackson.&nbsp;

00:05:24.080 --> 00:05:27.440
"Ladies first."
"Well then, after you."&nbsp;

00:05:28.400 --> 00:05:34.000
Season 9 also introduces a new race of villains&nbsp;
known as the Ori. These aliens discover the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:34.000 --> 00:05:38.160
existence of humans living in the Milky Way&nbsp;
galaxy, and they begin a violent crusade&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:38.160 --> 00:05:44.160
in our region of the universe. The Ori's ultimate&nbsp;
goal is to convert everyone to their religion:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:44.160 --> 00:05:49.680
Origin. Their highly advanced technology&nbsp;
forces SG-1 and Stargate Command to devise new&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:49.680 --> 00:05:55.280
and innovative ways to defeat this menacing foe.
Meanwhile, on Atlantis, the team there tries to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:55.280 --> 00:06:00.800
develop a retrovirus that will turn the Wraith&nbsp;
into humans. But the experiments aren't without&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:00.800 --> 00:06:06.240
flaws, with test subjects producing ambiguous&nbsp;
results at best. The Wraith, who feed on humans,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:06.240 --> 00:06:11.200
discover Earth's location and decide to head there&nbsp;
to use the population as a new feeding ground.

00:06:12.240 --> 00:06:17.440
Season 10 is the last hurrah for Stargate SG-1,&nbsp;
and the last time you'll watch two shows at the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:17.440 --> 00:06:22.640
same time. Being the last season of the series,&nbsp;
you'll get to see several major plotlines wrapped&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:22.640 --> 00:06:27.920
up in SG-1. Without giving anything major away,&nbsp;
the series finale ties up several threads,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:27.920 --> 00:06:32.400
including the fate of at least one fan-favorite&nbsp;
couple and the climax of the battle against one&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:32.400 --> 00:06:38.720
of the show's big bads. After dozens of episodes,&nbsp;
the final curtain closes on Stargate SG-1, so it's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:38.720 --> 00:06:44.080
time to head over to Stargate Atlantis season 3.
In Atlantis, the team manages to prevent the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:44.080 --> 00:06:48.400
Wraith from assaulting Earth, but they fail in&nbsp;
their attempts to develop a retrovirus to defeat&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:48.400 --> 00:06:53.360
their foe. The team on Atlantis continue&nbsp;
to battle the Wraith even as a new foe is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:53.360 --> 00:06:57.840
introduced in the form of self-replicating&nbsp;
nanobots that call themselves the Asurans.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:58.400 --> 00:07:03.200
These creatures threaten to destroy Atlantis,&nbsp;
so the team fires up the city's hyperdrives and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:03.200 --> 00:07:07.440
heads to the stars. You heard that right,&nbsp;
the entire city is a massive spaceship!&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:08.160 --> 00:07:13.040
Soon after Atlantis flees, it's badly damaged&nbsp;
and the crew find themselves adrift in space.

00:07:14.000 --> 00:07:17.520
Before moving on to the next season of&nbsp;
Stargate Atlantis, you should take a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:17.520 --> 00:07:21.920
couple of hours to watch the direct-to-video&nbsp;
movie Stargate: Ark of Truth, which picks&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:21.920 --> 00:07:26.880
up right after the end of Stargate SG-1.
Ark of Truth wraps up some dangling threads&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:26.880 --> 00:07:31.520
about the Ori left at the end of SG-1, and&nbsp;
effectively eliminates the enemy once and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:31.520 --> 00:07:36.080
for all. The movie opens by explaining the&nbsp;
existence of an ancient object known as the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:36.080 --> 00:07:41.840
Ark of Truth, a mysterious machine which has the&nbsp;
capabilities of defeating the Ori. Naturally,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:41.840 --> 00:07:46.880
the team is eager to find it. Unfortunately&nbsp;
for SG-1, it's located on the Ori's homeworld.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:46.880 --> 00:07:51.600
Despite it being a suicide mission, they visit the&nbsp;
planet and retrieve the device, but in the process&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:51.600 --> 00:07:56.240
resurrect an old enemy: The Replicators.
The Ori gather their forces for a final&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:56.240 --> 00:08:01.200
assault on our galaxy, but SG-1 activates&nbsp;
the Ark of Truth and defeats the Ori,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:01.200 --> 00:08:07.200
albeit in an unexpected way. See, the device&nbsp;
reveals to the Priors that the Ori are not&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:07.200 --> 00:08:13.200
gods. The Priors are humans who serve the Ori and&nbsp;
promote their religion, which includes plans to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:13.200 --> 00:08:18.720
invade Earth. The Ark of Truth causes all Priors&nbsp;
to become aware of the true nature of the Ori,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:18.720 --> 00:08:23.280
and they leave their religion, and abandon&nbsp;
the Ori all together. The movie ends with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:23.280 --> 00:08:28.320
SG-1 preparing to go through the Stargate on a&nbsp;
new mission, implying that the story will go on.

00:08:29.280 --> 00:08:33.600
With the Ark of Truth wrapped up, head back&nbsp;
to Stargate Atlantis and watch season 4.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:34.160 --> 00:08:37.200
There was some transition in the&nbsp;
Stargate franchise at this point.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:37.200 --> 00:08:41.680
For one, this is the first time Atlantis&nbsp;
aired as the only Stargate show on TV.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:42.720 --> 00:08:47.680
Secondly, the main cast shifted quite a bit.&nbsp;
Elizabeth Weir, played by Torri Higginson,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:47.680 --> 00:08:52.800
became incapacitated, which made room for Samantha&nbsp;
Carter to become a main character in the series.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:53.360 --> 00:08:58.320
Carter made the move from the SG-1 team,&nbsp;
and became a series regular on Atlantis.&nbsp;

00:08:58.320 --> 00:09:00.720
"Thanks for saving our asses&nbsp;
back there from the bad guys.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:02.400 --> 00:09:04.800
It was a risky move."
"It was nothing compared&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:04.800 --> 00:09:09.040
to the risk you and your team took."
The show's tone also took a darker turn&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:09.040 --> 00:09:14.320
this season. Season 4 opens with Atlantis still&nbsp;
adrift in space, and the team desperately trying&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:14.320 --> 00:09:19.200
to make repairs. They continue their two-front&nbsp;
war against both the Wraiths and the Asurans,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:19.200 --> 00:09:24.160
and part way through the season make the brilliant&nbsp;
move of pitting both enemies against each other.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:24.160 --> 00:09:28.400
The Atlantis team manage to reprogram the&nbsp;
Asurans, convincing them that the Wraiths&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:28.400 --> 00:09:32.480
are their enemies, and by the end of the&nbsp;
season the Wraiths are nearly wiped out.

00:09:33.440 --> 00:09:37.440
With only one season of Stargate Atlantis&nbsp;
remaining, it's time to take another break&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:37.440 --> 00:09:43.440
to watch the next standalone movie in the Stargate&nbsp;
SG-1 storyline. Stargate: Continuum occurs between&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:43.440 --> 00:09:49.760
seasons 4 and 5 of Atlantis and completes the&nbsp;
story arc of several characters from SG-1.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:49.760 --> 00:09:54.320
It revolves around one of the only survivors&nbsp;
of the Goa'uld after their defeat at the hands&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:54.320 --> 00:09:59.680
of Stargate Command. Ba'al, the last of the&nbsp;
Goa'uld System Lords survives the destruction&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:59.680 --> 00:10:05.120
of his people. He continued to play a minor role&nbsp;
in SG-1 during seasons 9 and 10, and occasionally&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:05.120 --> 00:10:09.680
joined forces with Stargate Command, but&nbsp;
ultimately remains a villainous figure.&nbsp;

00:10:09.680 --> 00:10:13.840
In Stargate: Continuum, the SG-1 team&nbsp;
finally corners Ba'al and plans to put&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:13.840 --> 00:10:18.400
a permanent end to him. However, it turns&nbsp;
out that this is merely a clone of Ba'al,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:18.400 --> 00:10:23.280
and the real System Lord has enacted&nbsp;
one last plan to gain universal power.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:23.280 --> 00:10:28.800
Ba'al time travels to 1939 and actually prevents&nbsp;
the Stargate program on Earth from ever happening.&nbsp;

00:10:29.360 --> 00:10:34.320
Doing so creates an alternate timeline where&nbsp;
Ba'al conquers the universe. As he readies an&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:34.320 --> 00:10:39.200
assault on Earth, a few members of SG-1 remember&nbsp;
the original timeline. Through their efforts,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:39.200 --> 00:10:43.840
they revert history back to its original course.&nbsp;
The movie ends how it started, with Ba'al about&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:43.840 --> 00:10:48.320
to be executed. This time, the characters are&nbsp;
unaware of the previous events or an alternate&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:48.320 --> 00:10:52.720
timeline. They complete the extraction process,&nbsp;
which brings an end to the Goa'uld for good.

00:10:53.600 --> 00:10:57.760
It's time to head back to Atlantis one more&nbsp;
time. The fifth season of Stargate Atlantis&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:57.760 --> 00:11:02.800
is the last. Fortunately, the show does a pretty&nbsp;
good job of wrapping up a bunch of plotlines.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:02.800 --> 00:11:07.360
McKay, the snobbish geek, finally falls in love&nbsp;
with Keller. The team defeats their archenemy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:07.360 --> 00:11:12.000
the Wraith. In the end, humans can finally&nbsp;
form a government in the Pegasus Galaxy,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:12.000 --> 00:11:17.040
free from the tyranny of enemy alien forces.
The series finale of Stargate Atlantis is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:17.040 --> 00:11:21.200
pretty spectacular. The Wraith discover the&nbsp;
location of Earth and head straight for it,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:21.200 --> 00:11:25.600
dinner being the only thing on their minds.&nbsp;
In response, the Atlantis team decides to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:25.600 --> 00:11:30.240
fly the city to Earth and join in a massive&nbsp;
fight to fend off the Wraith. After an epic&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:30.240 --> 00:11:35.600
battle and glorious victory, Atlantis lands in&nbsp;
the Pacific Ocean not far from San Francisco.

00:11:37.040 --> 00:11:42.160
The Stargate franchise continued after the end&nbsp;
of Atlantis in the show Stargate Universe, though&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:42.160 --> 00:11:47.280
this latest entry in the franchise only lasted two&nbsp;
seasons. Because it was the last of the series,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:47.280 --> 00:11:51.920
you can watch both in order without having to&nbsp;
split your attention with other shows and movies.&nbsp;

00:11:51.920 --> 00:11:56.160
The plot and characters are far removed from&nbsp;
the rest of the franchise, which makes the show&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:56.160 --> 00:12:01.040
its own independent story arc. In Stargate&nbsp;
Universe, humanity discovers an alien race&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:01.040 --> 00:12:06.480
called the Ancients. The Ancients sent a ship&nbsp;
deep into the unexplored parts of the universe.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:07.120 --> 00:12:12.560
The vessel traveled so far that it's actually&nbsp;
almost impossible to get to it using a Stargate.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:12.560 --> 00:12:17.040
And because the journey is so long, it's&nbsp;
basically a one-way trip. The ship doesn't&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:17.040 --> 00:12:21.760
have enough juice to send the travellers back.
A team from Stargate Command decides to take the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:21.760 --> 00:12:26.480
plunge, and they wind up stuck on the Ancient's&nbsp;
vessel. The show balances several storylines&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:26.480 --> 00:12:31.120
including trying to find a way to get home,&nbsp;
surviving this strange new place, and trying to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:31.120 --> 00:12:35.680
figure out what the Ancients wanted to accomplish&nbsp;
with the ship. It turns out, the craft was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:35.680 --> 00:12:40.160
investigating something incredibly close to the&nbsp;
point in the universe where the Big Bang occurred,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:40.160 --> 00:12:44.800
and there's evidence that life might have existed&nbsp;
before the beginning of the known universe.

00:12:45.920 --> 00:12:49.680
Up to this point, we've been going in&nbsp;
pretty much chronological order through&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:49.680 --> 00:12:54.720
the Stargate franchise. The last entry in&nbsp;
the list is the exception. Stargate Origins&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:54.720 --> 00:12:59.760
is actually a web series that serves as a prequel&nbsp;
of sorts to everything you've watched so far.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:59.760 --> 00:13:05.120
The series is set in 1939, long before the events&nbsp;
of the first movie. Origins is quite different&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:05.120 --> 00:13:10.640
from the rest of the shows. It only contains&nbsp;
ten episodes, and each is only ten minutes long.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:10.640 --> 00:13:14.240
After the initial release, every episode&nbsp;
was compiled into a single movie,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:14.240 --> 00:13:18.320
which is now available to stream. If you've&nbsp;
been binging all of the shows up to this point,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:18.320 --> 00:13:21.600
you should have no problem knocking&nbsp;
Stargate Origins out quickly.&nbsp;

00:13:21.600 --> 00:13:26.720
The plot follows Catherine Langford played by&nbsp;
Ellie Gall, who is trying to unlock the secrets&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:26.720 --> 00:13:31.440
of the Stargate. In SG-1, Langford is a minor&nbsp;
character and a good friend of Daniel Jackson.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:32.000 --> 00:13:35.760
It's explained throughout the series that&nbsp;
Langford was key in helping to establish&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:35.760 --> 00:13:40.720
the Stargate program. Now we get to see more&nbsp;
details about her story in Stargate Origins.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:40.720 --> 00:13:44.640
The main antagonist for this short&nbsp;
series is a Nazi who, surprise surprise,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:44.640 --> 00:13:49.040
knows about the Stargate and how it works.
Check out one of our newest videos right&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:49.040 --> 00:13:52.640
here! Plus, even more Looper videos about&nbsp;
your favorite shows are coming soon.&nbsp;&nbsp;

